  "details": "It has become increasingly common where newer players may have a very laggy experience with a full downloaded content cache, and not be aware this is the current impact. Increasing player education, and implementing a soft full downloaded content cache warning (controllable via toggle), or a visual indication of the max cache size such as 19.97gb/20gb based on the figuration can be helpful this way.\nAdditionally, it seems like a no brainer to have a setting to auto-clear the downloladed content cache when close to full, or when full on game close if the user opts for this option on top of the above suggestion.\nThere are of course situations where a user may want to mitigate re-downloading cached content, so allowing this as a toggle makes the most sense.\n\nTo be more explicitly clear, this is more along the lines of creating user facing functions that are seen here to clear once it reaches a certain size:\n\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/configuration-file#cache-settings",
